    {
      "id": "d3b5c2074deb0b74d525bc168da6627eef0ce327",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1140243179,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I have strong issues with switching back. Although I get that it will solve current issues, but at the same time it will not solve the current issues, just delays that we have to handle those, unless they are somehow resolved by Qt itself. I do not see that being happening, and so down the line we will be in the same situation again, just than we will have the issue twice, instead of once.\n\nI also not really sure, which issues the switch back really resolves? The issue with the additional characters was a change in the underlying functionality of the Qt type, which will not change over time. QMenu will also most certainly not change how it is implemented, as it is not seen as a mistake on Qt's side, bur rather an improvement on their part.\n\nSo I am not really sure what the move back should resolve (except user satisfaction) but at the same time I fear that it might lead to a prolonged move instead of a short (and admittedly painful) one.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2498449,
            "username": "rknall",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Roland Knall",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9e1d973c5007651b2ca47071f80324c2de5349d873e365cf0761df5542dfe382?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rknall"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-10-18T17:26:03.291Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-10-18T17:26:03.291Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 183387666,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 860017,
            "username": "geraldcombs",
